{
  "A set of options of which one is chosen: from plain values, from your own objects or from a live list; one under the other, side by side or in columns; options that are disabled, hidden or carry a help line; one Tab stop and the arrow keys.": "",
  "A plain value is its own text. `x-model` binds the chosen value two-way. Created with `new`, the same properties are set programmatically.": "",
  "Items from data": "",
  "Objects of your own shape take `itemText` and `itemValue` (a property name or a function). Plain or reactive, the items are read as they are: after adding, removing or renaming some in place, `refresh()` shows them, focus and choice kept.": "",
  "Disabled options, help lines, hints": "",
  "A `RadioItem` brings its own `enabled`, `visible`, `hint` and `helpText`, each a value or a function. The arrow keys skip what cannot be chosen.": "",
  "Orientation and columns": "",
  "Into the group, onto the chosen option (or the first one that can be chosen); the next Tab leaves the group.": "",
  "Moves to the next option and chooses it, wrapping from the last to the first; skips disabled and hidden options.": "",
  "The same, backwards. Right to left, ← and → swap.": "",
  "Chooses the focused option.": "",
  "Focuses the group (Control + Option + key on Apple platforms).": "",
  "`role=\"radiogroup\"`, named by the field label (`aria-labelledby`); `aria-orientation`, `aria-required`, `aria-readonly`, `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby` for the line under it.": "",
  "Native `<input type=\"radio\">` sharing a name, each inside its own `<label>`, drawn with `appearance: none`.": "",
  "An option’s `helpText` sits outside its label and describes it with `aria-describedby`, so it is not part of its name.": "",
  "Native `disabled`: skipped by the keyboard and read out as unavailable.": "",
  "One Tab stop; the design system focus ring, for the keyboard only.": "",
  "The group writes no text of its own: the option texts are yours (functions of your language state work). The `required` message comes from `uiLocale.strings`.": "",
  "The field. `data-orientation`, `data-columns`, `data-size`, `data-invalid`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`, `data-required`.": "",
  "The `radiogroup` element; `--_columns` and `--_rows` are set on it with `columns`.": "",
  "One option, and the label that holds its radio and text.": "",
  "The radio, its text, its help line.": "",
  "Units: the circle, with every state (`checked`, `invalid`, `hover`, `pressed`, `focus` and their pairs, `disabled`), and the dot of the chosen one (`checked`, `pressed`, `disabled`).": "",
  "Units: an option's row (`hover`, `checked`, `disabled`), its text and its help line.": "",
  "Units: a halo centred on the circle and a ring round an option under the keys, where the language has them.": "",
  "Units: the options together, and the group's label where it floats.": "",
  "The circle and the dot, per size and state.": "",
  "The row height (density tokens) and the text size.": "",
  "The space before the text, between options side by side, and above an option's help line.": "",
  "How far a press moves the circle, and what the ring under the keys goes round.": "",
  "The value of the chosen item; `null` when none is chosen. `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "The options. A function is followed: a new list shows at once; items changed in place show after `refresh()`.": "",
  "Where an item keeps its text, for objects of your own shape. A reader, not a binding.": "",
  "Where an item keeps its value. An object without one is its own value.": "",
  "The caption of the group; `&Name` makes Alt+N focus it. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "`top`, `side` (next to the options) or `hidden` (for screen readers only).": "",
  "`vertical`: one under the other; `horizontal`: side by side, wrapping.": "",
  "Lays the options out in a grid of this many columns (down the columns when vertical, across when horizontal).": "",
  "A line under the group. An error message takes its place.": "",
  "A tooltip on the group.": "",
  "The arrows move between the options, nothing can be chosen.": "",
  "One option must be chosen.": "",
  "generated": "",
  "The name the radios are sent with in a form.": "",
  "RadioItem": "",
  "What `value` becomes when this option is chosen.": "",
  "Shown next to the circle. Default: the value as text.": "",
  "A smaller line under the text; it describes the radio.": "",
  "`false` greys it out; the arrow keys skip it.": "",
  "`false` leaves it out.": "",
  "The element with `role=\"radiogroup\"`.": "",
  "The native radios, in the order of the items.": "",
  "Focuses the chosen option, or the first one that can be chosen.": "",
  "Your items may be plain or reactive; the group reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. Their texts, values and states are read again; focus stays where it is.": "",
  "The DOM events of the radios reach the group.": ""
}
